/* book exam traps: Assuming 100 % fault coverage means zero escapes. T counts only the faults the model lists; a defect the model does not describe can still escape. | Swapping yield and fault coverage. Yield is a property of the fab (good die out of all die); fault coverage is a property of the test program (faults detected out of faults listed). | Mixing up the chain: a defect is physical, a fault is its logical model, an error is a wrong node value, a failure is lost function. | A unit slip in DPM: DL = 0.005 is 5000 DPM. Multiply by 10⁶, not 10⁴. | Saying verification proves the chip works. Simulation checks the design; only the tester checks each manufactured copy. */
